# The build context is the repository root (the Dockerfile COPYs
# pyproject.toml and poetry.lock from it), and without this every one of these
# is uploaded to the daemon on each build. `.venv` alone is the bulk of it,
# and it is the one that would also be actively wrong to carry in: a venv
# built against the host's interpreter and paths.
.venv/
.git/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
__pycache__/
dist/
site/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
config.yaml
docker/.env
docker/claude/
